                <pb facs="0640" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg566"/>

                <head>Mr. Hale to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 16.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States of
                                America</hi>. <hi rendition="#italic">Madrid,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 18, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Although the rebellion or insurrection has
                    not as yet been entirely suppressed by the Spanish government, yet everything
                    that I can see, hear, or learn, from any source, confirms me in the opinion
                    which I ventured to express in my despatch to you, No. 15, of January 9. Madrid
                    has been perfectly quiet and tranquil from the beginning, and so continues to
                    the present moment. The two houses of the national Cortes continued their daily
                    sessions here regularly, and there is nothing which meets the eye to indicate
                    the slightest disturbance of the public tranquillity. I have had several
                    communications from Americans visiting in other parts of Europe, inquiring if it
                    were perfectly safe to visit Spain at the present time, and I have uniformly
                    answered that it was.</p>
                <p>With much respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN P. HALE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
